<title>POLAND: Polish food prices rise 0.1 pct in Feb 10-20.</title>
<headline>Polish food prices rise 0.1 pct in Feb 10-20.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish food prices rose 0.1 percent in the February 10-20 period after rising 0.1 percent in the previous 10 days and were 0.4 percent higher than in the January 10-20 period, the Central Statistical Office said.  </p>
<p>				    FEB 10-20   FEB 1-10   LAST 30 DAYS</p>
<p>POLISH FOOD PRICES (AVG)	0.1	   0.1	  0.4 (0.5)</p>
<p> Bread				0.3	   0.9	  1.6 (1.8)</p>
<p> Fruit and vegetables	  -0.5	  -1.1	 -1.6 (-0.6)</p>
<p> Meat and meat-products	-0.1	  -0.2	 -0.4 (-0.2)</p>
<p> Dairy products		   0.4	   0.6	  1.8 (1.5)</p>
<p> Eggs				-1.1	  -1.6	 -2.9 (-2.0)</p>
<p>NOTE: Figures in brackets figures are for the previous 30-day period ending on February 10.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
